<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pathet Lao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>–<a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pathet Lao was the communist movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, founded in 1950 under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souphanouvong">Souphanouvong</a> with the support of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>. It fought the Royal Lao Government in a long civil war that became part of the wider <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> conflict. In 1975 it took power, abolished the monarchy and founded the Lao People's Democratic Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pathet-lao.jpg" alt="Pathet Lao" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Laos.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
